cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper and its record as below."
title: "Gubernaut: A Deterministic Homeostatic Controller for Affect-Regulated LLM Agents, Validated Across Independent Model Families"
# A person, not an organization. The previous `- name: "Gubernaut Research"` form
# declares an ENTITY; Zenodo read it as a personal name and split it, rendering the
# author as "Research, Gubernaut". People need given-names/family-names.
authors:
  - given-names: "Dushyant"
    family-names: "Sharma"
    affiliation: "Gubernaut Research"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6534-0347"
    email: "dushyant@gubernaut.com"
year: 2026
license: CC-BY-4.0
# The CONCEPT DOI: it always resolves to the newest archived version. Never put a
# version DOI here — it pins every reader to whichever release happened to be first.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21303518
url: "https://gubernaut.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thegubernaut/Gubernaut_Validation"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21303518
    description: "Concept DOI — resolves to the latest archived version"
  - type: url
    value: "https://gubernaut.com/paper/gubernaut_whitepaper.pdf"
    description: "White paper (camera-ready PDF)"
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - runtime control layer
  - homeostatic regulation
  - metacognition
  - affect regulation
  - cognitive governor
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - cross-family evaluation
  - prompt injection
  - AI safety
  - pre-registration
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered, cross-family, generate-once / judge-many evaluation of a
  deterministic runtime control layer for LLM agents. Four frontier models
  (GPT-5.5, Claude Opus 4.8, Gemini 3.5 Flash, Grok 4.3), each serving as both
  generator and judge, form a symmetric 4x4 matrix: the regulated arm is calmer
  in 15 of 16 cells by sign (11 of 12 off-diagonal) and 13 of 16 at p<.05, with
  the one null cell (-0.04, GPT x Gemini) reported alongside the headline; the
  recovery signature replicates 4/4. The three sub-threshold cells all fall on
  the single near-saturated host. The effect survives a lineage-independent
  fourth judge family. The earlier three-model matrix was pre-registered and
  frozen before the fourth family was added; adding it changed no earlier cell,
  and both ship verbatim. Transcripts, judge panels (SHA-256), and the combine
  script are published so the result is independently recomputable. No
  consciousness claims are made.
